WEBVTT

00:00:02.521 --> 00:00:05.024
HAGRID: Did you bring
your father's cloak, like I asked you?

00:00:05.274 --> 00:00:07.610
HARRY: Yeah, I brought the cloak.
Hagrid, where are we going?

00:00:07.776 --> 00:00:09.236
You'll see soon enough.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.530
Now pay attention, this is important.

00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:14.742
What's with the flower?

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:18.329
Hagrid, have you combed your hair?

00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:20.331
As a matter of fact, I have.

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:23.751
You might like to try the same thing
now and again.

00:00:24.293 --> 00:00:26.921
[DISTANT ROARING]

00:00:28.172 --> 00:00:30.299
[SNARLING]

00:00:32.343 --> 00:00:33.677
MAXIME:
Hagrid?

00:00:37.556 --> 00:00:39.391
The cloak! Put the cloak on!

00:00:46.148 --> 00:00:49.401
-Bonsoir, Olympe.
-Oh, Hagrid.

00:00:49.568 --> 00:00:53.364
I thought perhaps you weren't coming.
I thought perhaps...

00:00:53.447 --> 00:00:56.283
...you had forgotten me.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:58.369
Couldn't forget you, Olympe.

00:00:59.036 --> 00:01:00.704
-Ugh.
-What is it you wanted to show me?

00:01:02.414 --> 00:01:05.709
When we spoke earlier,
you sounded so...

00:01:06.085 --> 00:01:07.461
...exhilarated.

00:01:08.212 --> 00:01:10.965
You'll be glad you came. Trust me.

00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.093
[ROARING]

00:01:14.343 --> 00:01:16.345
[SPEAKS IN FRENCH]

00:01:21.475 --> 00:01:23.394
MAXIME:
Can we get closer?

00:01:31.193 --> 00:01:32.486
Dragons?

00:01:32.736 --> 00:01:34.363
That's the first task?

00:01:34.613 --> 00:01:36.573
-You're joking.
HAGRID: Come on, Harry.

00:01:37.992 --> 00:01:40.995
These are seriously
misunderstood creatures.

00:01:42.121 --> 00:01:43.497
Oh, crikey!

00:01:44.206 --> 00:01:46.250
Although, I have to admit...

00:01:46.417 --> 00:01:49.253
...that Horntail is a right nasty
piece of work.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:52.214
Poor Ron nearly fainted
just seeing him, you know.

00:01:53.632 --> 00:01:55.718
-Ron was here?
-Oh, sure.

00:01:55.884 --> 00:01:59.430
His brother Charlie helped
to bring him over from Romania.

00:01:59.513 --> 00:02:01.015
Didn't Ron tell you that?

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:04.435
No, he didn't.

00:02:05.144 --> 00:02:07.021
He didn't tell me a thing.

00:02:16.905 --> 00:02:20.034
BOY 1: You cheat, Potter.
BOY 2: You stink, Potter.

00:02:21.452 --> 00:02:24.288
-Good luck, Potter.
BOY 3: Potter stinks!

00:02:24.455 --> 00:02:27.041
-Cedric rules.
HARRY: Thanks.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.793
Like the badge?

00:02:30.419 --> 00:02:32.129
Excuse me.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.676
BOY 1:
Harry.

00:02:38.427 --> 00:02:40.304
Hey! Read the badge, Potter!

00:02:40.471 --> 00:02:41.930
Can I have a word?

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.683
-All right.
BOY 2: You stink, Potter!

00:02:44.933 --> 00:02:47.936
BOY 3: Potter, you stink!
BOY 4: Harry Potter smells!

00:02:50.481 --> 00:02:52.941
Dragons. That's the first task.

00:02:53.192 --> 00:02:56.403
-They've got one for each of us.
BOY 2: Come on, Ced!

00:02:56.487 --> 00:02:58.489
Are you serious?

00:02:59.323 --> 00:03:02.409
And Fleur and Krum, do they--?

00:03:02.493 --> 00:03:04.536
-Yes.
BOY 2: Come on, Ced, leave him.

00:03:04.703 --> 00:03:06.413
CEDRIC: Right.
BOY 2: He's not worth it.

00:03:06.497 --> 00:03:09.166
BOY 1: Read the badges, Potter!
-Hey, listen. About the badges.

00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:12.336
-I've asked them not to wear them, but--
-Don't worry about it.

00:03:12.503 --> 00:03:14.838
It's not like I try
to blow things up, exactly.

00:03:15.506 --> 00:03:17.049
It just happens a fair bit.

00:03:17.216 --> 00:03:20.344
You have to admit, though,
fire's pretty fascinating.

00:03:20.511 --> 00:03:22.346
You're a right foul git, you know that?

00:03:22.513 --> 00:03:24.598
-You think so?
-I know so.

00:03:24.848 --> 00:03:26.225
Anything else?

00:03:26.475 --> 00:03:29.853
-Yeah. Stay away from me.
-Fine.

00:03:32.314 --> 00:03:35.859
CRABBE: There's Potter. Cheat.
MALFOY: Why so tense, Potter?

00:03:36.527 --> 00:03:38.987
My father and I have a bet, you see.

00:03:39.238 --> 00:03:42.491
I don't think you're gonna last
10 minutes in this tournament.

00:03:44.952 --> 00:03:47.830
He disagrees.
He thinks you won't last five.

00:03:47.996 --> 00:03:51.208
I don't give a damn
what your father thinks, Malfoy.

00:03:52.209 --> 00:03:56.213
He's vile and cruel.
And you're just pathetic.

00:03:57.131 --> 00:03:59.550
-Pathetic?
-Oh, no, you don't, sonny!

00:03:59.758 --> 00:04:01.260
Aah!

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.638
MOODY: I'll teach you to curse someone
when their back is turned!

00:04:04.888 --> 00:04:08.642
You stinking, cowardly, scummy...

00:04:08.892 --> 00:04:10.561
-Professor Moody!
-...back-shooting--

00:04:10.769 --> 00:04:13.647
-What are you doing?
-Teaching.

00:04:14.648 --> 00:04:18.360
-Is that a--? Is that a student?
-Technically, it's a ferret.

00:04:18.527 --> 00:04:20.654
Oh! Ah!

00:04:24.575 --> 00:04:26.535
Stand still! Stand still!

00:04:37.546 --> 00:04:39.590
-My father will hear about this!
-Is that a threat?

00:04:39.756 --> 00:04:41.675
-Professor Moody!
-Is that a threat?

00:04:41.884 --> 00:04:43.760
Professor!

00:04:43.927 --> 00:04:47.514
I could tell you stories about your father
that would curl even your greasy hair!

00:04:47.598 --> 00:04:50.434
-Alastor! Alastor.
-It doesn't end here!

00:04:50.601 --> 00:04:54.438
We never use transfiguration
as a punishment!

00:04:54.605 --> 00:04:56.648
Surely Dumbledore told you that.

00:04:57.316 --> 00:05:01.653
-He might've mentioned it.
-Well, you will do well to remember it.

00:05:02.779 --> 00:05:04.323
Away!

00:05:07.451 --> 00:05:09.620
You. Come with me.

00:05:14.625 --> 00:05:16.627
[GRUNTS]

00:05:18.212 --> 00:05:19.630
[GROANS]

00:05:44.738 --> 00:05:46.865
That's a Foe-Glass.

00:05:47.658 --> 00:05:49.660
Lets me keep an eye on my enemies.

00:05:50.244 --> 00:05:54.665
If I can see the whites of their eyes,
they're standing right behind me.

00:05:54.748 --> 00:05:57.876
[RUMBLING]
[DISTANT SHOUTING]

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.255
Wouldn't even bother telling you
what's in there.

00:06:01.505 --> 00:06:03.507
You wouldn't believe it if I did.

00:06:03.674 --> 00:06:05.509
Now...

00:06:07.094 --> 00:06:09.888
...what are you going to do
about your dragon?

00:06:10.097 --> 00:06:12.683
Oh, um....

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:16.144
Well, you know, I just thought I'd....

00:06:17.688 --> 00:06:19.106
Sit.

00:06:22.734 --> 00:06:24.152
Listen to me, Potter.

00:06:25.153 --> 00:06:26.405
Your pal Diggory?

00:06:26.655 --> 00:06:30.909
By your age, he could turn a whistle into
a watch and have it sing you the time.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:33.495
Miss Delacour?

00:06:33.745 --> 00:06:36.665
She's as much a fairy princess as I am.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:40.627
As for Krum, his head
may be filled with sawdust...

00:06:40.711 --> 00:06:42.921
...but Karkaroff's is not.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.923
They'll have a strategy.

00:06:45.132 --> 00:06:48.677
And you can bet that it will
play to Krum's strengths.

00:06:53.515 --> 00:06:54.933
Come on, Potter.

00:06:55.183 --> 00:06:57.311
What are your strengths?

00:06:57.519 --> 00:06:58.687
Um....

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.188
I don't know.

00:07:00.439 --> 00:07:03.191
Well, I can fly.
I mean, I'm a fair flyer. But I....

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:07.446
-Better than fair, the way I heard it.
-But I'm not allowed a broom.

00:07:07.696 --> 00:07:11.199
You're allowed a wand.

00:07:17.706 --> 00:07:19.041
FRED:
Bets! Place your bets!

00:07:19.207 --> 00:07:21.460
GEORGE:
Bets taken! Bets taken here!

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.588
Step up, folks! Who fancies a flutter
in today's bloodbath?

00:07:24.755 --> 00:07:27.591
Smart money's on Krum to survive!
Any bets?

00:07:27.758 --> 00:07:29.217
Yes, sir?

00:07:29.718 --> 00:07:32.220
Ten-to-1 for Fleur. There you go.
Thank you very much.

00:07:32.763 --> 00:07:32.767
DUMBLEDORE:
Your attention, please.

